The '''2000 Football League Cup final''' was played between [[Leicester City F.C.|Leicester City]], in their third final appearance in four years, and [[Football League Division One|First Division]] side [[Tranmere Rovers F.C.|Tranmere Rovers]] at [[Wembley Stadium (1923)|Wembley Stadium]] on 27 February 2000. It was the 34th and last League Cup final to be played at the original Wembley Stadium.<ref>{{cite web |first=James M. |last=Ross |title=England - Football League Cup Finals |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tablese/engleagcuphist.html |website=Rec.Sport.Soccer Statistics Foundation |date=29 April 2021 |access-date=14 May 2021 |archive-date=29 June 2012 |archive-url=https://archive.today/20120629080535/http://www.rsssf.com/tablese/engleagcuphist.html |url-status=live }}</ref> Leicester won 2–1 to become the last team to win the League Cup at the old Wembley.<ref>{{cite web|url= https://www.fourfourtwo.com/features/where-are-they-now-leicester-citys-2000-league-cup-winners|title= Where are they now? Leicester City's 2000 League Cup winners|work=fourfourtwo|access-date=27 April 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url= https://news.bbc.co.uk/2/hi/sport/football/659113.stm|title= Leicester set sights on Europe|date=27 February 2000|work=BBC Sport|access-date=27 April 2017}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |url=https://www.bbc.co.uk/sport/football/56817786 |title=Leicester City: The inside story of La Manga and the Foxes last cup final |publisher=BBC Sport |date=14 May 2021 |accessdate=14 May 2021 |first=Neil |last=Johnston }}</ref>

